# NetworkPolicy webblock-tenant-network for one tenant namespace on the k3d engine (spike design
# .claude/docs/designs/k3s-site-cluster-spike.md G8): the kube-router form of tenant-network.yaml.tmpl.
# kube-router enforces only Kubernetes NetworkPolicy, which is namespaced, so there is one per
# wb-<projectId> namespace instead of one cluster-wide policy. No FR asks for tenant network isolation
# yet (design section 11, Q1), so nothing in Provisioning writes it: the live test
# tests/integration/stack/test_tenant_network_k3s_live.py applies it to its own test tenants only.
# Placeholders: @NAMESPACE@ (the tenant namespace) and @CATALOG_IP@ (the address of the container
# webblock-catalog-db on the kind Docker network).
#
# A pod selected by a policy of both types is default-deny in both directions, so the rules below are
# the whole of what a site may do:
#   ingress  only from Traefik (the Gateway, app.kubernetes.io/name=traefik in kube-system); kubelet
#            probes rely on kube-router admitting traffic from the pod's own node;
#   egress   to the catalog PostgreSQL on TCP 5432, to the cluster DNS (k8s-app=kube-dns in
#            kube-system) on port 53 UDP and TCP, and through the Gateway to any site, as any client
#            could: to Traefik's pods on its entry point ports 8000 and 8443 (the Service's 80 and 443
#            after translation).
# Unlike the Cilium policy there is no egressDeny: the metadata address 169.254.169.254 is refused
# because nothing allows it. Everything else is refused too: other tenants' pods (also by their own
# ingress rule), the Kubernetes API server, the image registry and the other containers on the kind
# network.
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: webblock-tenant-network
  namespace: @NAMESPACE@
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: webblock-provisioning
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
    - Egress
  ingress:
    - from:
        - namespaceSelector:
            matchLabels:
              kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system
          podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app.kubernetes.io/name: traefik
  egress:
    - to:
        - ipBlock:
            cidr: @CATALOG_IP@/32
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 5432
    - to:
        - namespaceSelector:
            matchLabels:
              kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system
          podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              k8s-app: kube-dns
      ports:
        - protocol: UDP
          port: 53
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 53
    - to:
        - namespaceSelector:
            matchLabels:
              kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system
          podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app.kubernetes.io/name: traefik
      ports:
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 8000
        - protocol: TCP
          port: 8443
